Sorry, here it is! The script is the one you posted but with "polygonX", with mine the crash was the same:

  library(secr)
  setwd('C:/Users/Rob/Documents/R')
  vertici <- read.traps ('buffer2vertici.txt', detector = 'polygonX')

  capt <- read.table ('captXY.txt')
  ch <- make.capthist (capt, vertici, fmt = 'XY')
  msk <- make.mask(vertici, buffer = 6000, type = 'trapbuffer')
  fit <- secr.fit(ch, mask = msk)
  fit

Before maximization I have an expected

Warning message:
In make.capthist(capt, vertici, fmt = "XY") :
  dropping repeat detections within occasions at exclusive detectors (traps)

Then, just after the first maximization, it crashes as in "RCrash.jpg". The error message in italian says "R for Windows GUI has stopped working", then I can choose to look online for a solution or quit the program.

I will make some trials as you suggested, thanx!

Roberto

